<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konstanty Ostrogski</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1460–1530</span> · Also known as Kostiantyn Ostrozkyi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Konstanty Ostrogski was a Ruthenian prince and Grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hetman">Hetman</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>. Captured by the Muscovites at Vedrosha in 1500, he escaped and later won many victories over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatars</a> and, in 1514, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-orsha">Battle of Orsha</a> over a larger Muscovite army. An <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a>, he was a leading patron of the Orthodox Church within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/konstanty-ostrogski.jpg" alt="Konstanty Ostrogski" width="320" height="377" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kanstantyn_Astroski._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BD%D1%82%D1%8B%D0%BD_%D0%90%D1%81%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BA%D1%96_(XVIII).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
